# Errors memcheck reports in code outside TuringDB, in valgrind's suppression format.

# mimalloc, which Arrow bundles as its allocator: at load time it reads the transparent huge
# page setting into a stack buffer, then scans the buffer past the bytes the read filled.
{
   mimalloc-scans-the-huge-page-setting-past-the-read
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:_mi_strnstr
   fun:_mi_prim_mem_init
   fun:mi_process_init*
   fun:_mi_auto_process_init
}
